  <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Starting early is the most powerful factor in compound growth, even with smaller contributions.</li>
    <li>The more frequently interest compounds, the faster your money grows over time.</li>
    <li>Consistent contributions and reinvesting earnings maximize the compounding effect.</li>
    <li>Use the Rule of 72 for quick mental estimates of how long it takes your money to double.</li>
  </ul>
